# Pairs with NoFalseAbsence. The movement check counts a trimmed history
# window (or one whose first surviving entry is an old-clock replay) as
# complete, so an absent anchor whose create and later delete fell outside
# the window reads as unmoved, and the reconciler records a committed create
# whose caller crashed as not committed.
MODULE: AuditTrimmedWindowCountsAsComplete
TARGET: NoFalseAbsence
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a trimmed history window is taken as proof that the anchor never moved
PERTURBS: Reconcile

--- FIND
                    ELSE IF Obs # 0 THEN "Moved"
                    ELSE IF ~viewComplete THEN "Unproven"
--- REPLACE
                    ELSE IF Obs # 0 THEN "Moved"
                    ELSE IF ~viewComplete THEN "Unmoved"
--- END
